# scaling-phantoms.vrs: scaling D21 (Session 2), several players in game. A Debug build with [Debug] FaultInjection
# `scaleplayers:3@40` adds three phantom counted players of gear level 40 beside Chaos at each scaled read (Debug builds
# only, S-13), so with [Scoreboard] IncludeAdmins = true every decision counts 4 players at an average of
# round((g + 120) / 4). [Limits] MaxUnitsPerWave = 8 for this run, so the scaled waves are also clamped.
# (a) sc-wave (tools/vrclient/fixtures/sc-wave.json) at sc-a logs "players 4, gear A, level A+2, units 4 -> 10" and
#     "clamped by MaxUnitsPerWave: 10 -> 8"; `.nyar debug here 40` lists 8 thugs at level A+2.
# (b) sc-region (fixtures/sc-region.json: a Region location over FarbaneWoods, 4 CHAR_Spider_Forest) logs its scaled
#     count "units 4 -> 10" before its "in <g> groups over FarbaneWoods" line.
# (c) apo-test with the block (fixtures/sc-apo.json: apo-test plus scaling 2/true/2/0) logs at its start
#     "scaling apo-test roamers: players 4, per hotspot 9, max …" (3 + 6) and, at horde 1 (1 min in),
#     "scaling apo-test horde 1: players 4, gear A, level A+2, units 8 -> 14" (size 8 + 6 regular units).
# The cfg and the FaultInjection value are restored after the session (snapshot restore).
#
# Needs: a Debug DLL with scaling step 3; sc-wave, sc-region and apo-test (sc-apo.json) enabled, every other spawning
# definition disabled; [Debug] FaultInjection = scaleplayers:3@40; [Scoreboard] IncludeAdmins = true; [Limits]
# MaxUnitsPerWave = 8; NyarDevTools (.devtp, .devgear, .devkill) and DevChatEcho; no purge cooldown; Chaos invulnerable
# (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean, never false).
# Run: --var AX=-1880 --var AZ=-1640
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .devtp ${AX} ${AZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devgear
expect-log \[DEV GEAR\] armor=[0-9.]+ spell=[0-9.]+ weapon=[0-9.]+ sum=[0-9.]+ full=[0-9.]+ floor=(?P<G>[0-9]+)
calc A = floor((${G} + 120) / 4 + 0.5)
calc L1 = ${A} + 2
# (a) sc-wave: 4 players, 10 asked, 8 by the cap
mark
chat .nyar event start sc-wave
expect-log event sc-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
expect-seen scaling phantoms: 3 of 3 at gear 40
expect-seen \[nyar\] scaling sc-wave wave 1: players 4, gear ${A}, level ${L1}, units 4 -> 10
expect-seen clamped by MaxUnitsPerWave: 10 -> 8
wait 8
chat .nyar debug here 40
expect-log CHAR_Bandit_Thug sc-wave left [0-9]+s lvl ${L1}
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 8 (
chat .nyar event info sc-wave
expect-reply scaling now: 4 players, gear ${A}, level ${L1}
shot full sc-phantoms-wave
chat .nyar event stop sc-wave
expect-log event sc-wave stopped
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
# (b) sc-region: the scaled count before the groups
mark
chat .nyar event start sc-region
expect-log in [0-9]+ groups over FarbaneWoods timeout=30
expect-seen \[nyar\] scaling sc-region wave 1: players 4, gear ${A}, level ${L1}, units 4 -> 10
shot full sc-phantoms-region
chat .nyar event stop sc-region
expect-log event sc-region stopped
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
# (c) apo-test with the block: roamers at the start, horde 1 a minute in
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
expect-seen \[nyar\] scaling apo-test roamers: players 4, per hotspot 9, max [0-9]+ timeout=30
expect-log \[nyar\] scaling apo-test horde 1: players 4, gear ${A}, level ${L1}, units 8 -> 14 timeout=120
shot full sc-phantoms-apo
chat .nyar event stop apo-test
expect-log event apo-test stopped
# the stop's despawns are staged through the per-tick budget
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=60
console TPHome
wait 3
